          %h2#history History
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HomePage"} nLab
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                collaborative
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wiki"} wiki
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2007/09/towards_a_higherdimensional_wi.html"} I
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2008/11/beyond_the_blog.html"} II
            = succeed "Lab\u201D)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/"}
                The
                = succeed "-Category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/philosophy"} philosophy
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+structures"} higher structures
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-point+of+view"} point of view
            of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+theory"} type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+algebra"} higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+algebra"} categorical algebra
            (the “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            ” in “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            Lab” and “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nPOV"}> nPOV
            ”).
          %p
            The
            = succeed "Lab" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/2008/11/nlab.html"} created
            in November 2008 by
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacques+Distler"} Jacques Distler
            = succeed "Lab\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-Category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "\u2018s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"} John Baez
          %p
            Discussion of and around edits to the
            = succeed "Lab" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a{:href => "https://nforum.ncatlab.org/"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              Forum
            which roughly plays the role of the “talk”-pages at Wikipedia.
          %h2#what_the_lab_is
            What the
            = succeed "Lab" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            The most apt analogy for the
            = succeed "Lab" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "." do
              %strong group lab book
          %ul
            %li Notes from seminars
            %li Notes from papers and books
            %li Summaries of known work
            %li Observations and results from experiments
            %li Ideas for future work
          %p
            Apart from not having actual physical experiments, this matches the content of the
            = succeed "Lab" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "Lab" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %ol
            %li To enable others to benefit from our work while it is still being done.
            %li To benefit from the work of others while we are doing it.
          %p There is much more to a research project than that which appears in the final paper and we believe that since our results and our final proofs will be public, then both we and those who might read such a paper can benefit from beginning the interaction much earlier in its development.
          %p Thus by making our lab book public, we hope that casual passers-by will stop, read, and scribble something on it that will help us do our research.
          %p There are three things to say about this that are worth making very clear.
          %ol
            %li
              Our reasons for having the
              = succeed "Lab" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %li
              But to make it
              %em work
              properly in public, we need to make it attractive to others so that they will stop by, read our jottings, and scribble something of their own.
            %li We aim to achieve a system whereby those who put most in are also those who get most out.
          %h2#who_are_we Who Are We?
          %p
            The
            = succeed "Lab" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category/"}
              The
              = succeed "-Category" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            and the loose-knit community surrounding that blog. It is not possible to give a precise description of who is in that community, and the community involved in the
            = succeed "Lab" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %ol
            %li
              To join, you need to be willing to interact with the group and material already present, from the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-point+of+view"} n-point of view
              = succeed "Lab" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "Lab" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %li
              We will ask you to leave if what you are doing has little connection with what the rest of the group is doing and if it is interfering with others trying to do their work. This is of course unpleasant, since most people who come to contribute do so with honorable intentions. To help minimize possible areas of friction, it may help to read
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/writing+in+the+nLab"} writing in the nLab
          %h2#in_practice In Practice?
          %p
            The way that this is being worked out in practice is as follows. Currently it seems that common motivations for contributing to the
            = succeed "Lab" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                to
                %strong assemble information
                on
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/philosophy"} philosophy
                in a modern unified way, from the perspective of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+category+theory"} higher category theory
            %li
              %p
                to
                %strong provide exposition
                of this information which is useful to a wide range of readers of differing expertise;
            %li
              %p
                to jointly
                %strong develop ideas
                and research on applying higher categorical concepts and tools to issues in
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/philosophy"} philosophy
          %p To some extent this involves
          %ul
            %li
              collecting in principle “well known” definitions and facts in an encyclopaedic fashion, to the extent that these are not readily available, or not in the desired form, for instance on
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Main_Page"} Wikipedia
              %em could
              eventually develop into something like a modern version of a
              = succeed "-like" do
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bourbaki"} Bourbaki
              = succeed "Lab" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            But on top of this encyclopaedic function, and hopefully in parallel to that, the
            = succeed "Lab" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %ul
            %li
              intended as providing a
              %em laboratory
              for collaborative development of ideas – for research. Within the community out of which the
              = succeed "Lab" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematics"} mathematics
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/philosophy"} philosophy
              = succeed "Lab" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "Lab" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p These points together imply that
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                on the
                = succeed "Lab" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %em right
                perspectives, definitions and explanations from a modern unified higher categorical perspective;
            %li
              %p at the same time we want to indicate clearly which part of an entry is traditional common material, which is a modern but widely-accepted reformulation and which is genuinely the result of original research by a contributor or by several contributors;
            %li
              %p
                we will intersperse possibly controversial but always constructive
                %strong discussion
                into entries if we feel the need. While in general the
                %a{:href => "http://golem.ph.utexas.edu/category"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  \-Category Café
                is where we have chat and discussion and the
                = succeed "Lab" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                = succeed "Lab" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                = succeed "Lab" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HowTo"} HowTo
                page.
          %h2#what_the_lab_is_not
            What the
            = succeed "Lab" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            Most importantly the
            = succeed "Lab" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %ul
            %li
              %strong not complete
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %strong not meant to be complete
              = succeed "!" do
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Stub"} stubs
          %p
            %strong> If you find yourself annoyed by the state any given entry is in
            , for whatever reason, please feel encouraged to edit it in order to improve the situation.
          %p
            %strong> Notice
            \: an entry being in a pitiful state is usually more a sign of nobody having spared the time and energy to work on it, than of our joint incompetence to write a decent entry if we were being paid for doing it. So if you find your eyebrows raised by some entry, don’t turn away to be the next one
            %em not
            to work on it. Instead, improve it. We all do this voluntarily. We all have other duties to look after. So don’t be annoyed with “us”, help us.
          %p
            So if you feel existing material needs to be changed, you can do so. If you feel further material needs to be added, different perspectives need to be amplified, you can add a new paragraph, headed by a suitable headline.
            = succeed ":" do
              %strong Be bold
            = succeed "Lab" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            See the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HowTo"} HowTo
            page for information on how to contribute to the
            = succeed "Lab" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %h2#organization_of_the_lab
            Organization of the
            = succeed "Lab" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %ul
            %li
              see
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/HomePage"} HomePage
          %h2#technology_and_support Technology and Support
          %p
            Historically, the nlab was powered by
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "https://golem.ph.utexas.edu/wiki/instiki/show/HomePage"} Instiki
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "https://github.com/ncatlab/nlab"} custom fork
            %a{:href => "https://nforum.ncatlab.org/21/"} nLab Technical Matters
            at the nForum, but can also be posted
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "https://github.com/ncatlab/nlab/issues"} at github
          %p
            The physical server running the nLab lives at
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "http://www.cmu.edu"} Carnegie Mellon University
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            MURI award FA9550-15-1-0053 from the United States Air Force Office of Scientific Research. Any opinions, findings and conclusions or recommendations expressed on the nLab are those of the authors and do not necessarily reflect the views of the AFOSR.
